Social media is a public good, in the sense that it provides a benefit(access to information and public discourse) to those who use it, and in that its continued existence depends upon people using and posting to it(see also the [network effect](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Network_effect)). All major social media platforms, though, are owned and operated by private companies, which aren't obligated have to have consumer interests in mind!

